                          <TR>
                            <TD><A name=3Dtop></A>
                              <P>Forgery of documents is becoming easier =
than=20
                              ever before with the advancement being =
made in the=20
                              technology of computers, scanners, =
printers and=20
                              copiers. The problem does not only exist =
with=20
                              check forgery but also with other =
documents that=20
                              have dollar value or data value associated =
with=20
                              them. The examples below give you an idea =
of some=20
                              security problems that can occur on =
different=20
                              documents.<BR>&nbsp;</P>
                              <DIV align=3Dcenter>
                              <CENTER>
                              <TABLE cellSpacing=3D0 cellPadding=3D0 =
width=3D611=20
                              border=3D0>
                                <TBODY>
                                <TR>
                                <TD width=3D402>
                                <P align=3Dcenter><IMG height=3D172=20
                                =
src=3D"http://glossary.ippaper.com/images/graphicsedviser/common/security=
/ProbChecks.jpg"=20
                                width=3D407 border=3D0> </P></TD>
                                <TD vAlign=3Dtop width=3D200>
                                <P align=3Dcenter><B>Checks</B></P>
                                <P>Checks can be forged in several ways. =
Because=20
                                of the advancement of technology in =
computers,=20
                                scanners, printers and copiers, checks =
that do=20
                                not have the proper security features, =
can be=20
                                duplicated so that it is hard to tell =
the=20
                                difference between the duplicated check =
and the=20
                                original. </P></TD></TR>
                                <TR>
                                <TD vAlign=3Dtop width=3D609 =
colSpan=3D2>
                                <P><BR>Another type of forgery that =
occurs on=20
                                checks is the alteration of the dollar =
amount or=20
                                the name of the payee on the check. This =

                                alteration is accomplished by a couple =
of=20
                                different methods. If the check is =
printed=20
                                through a printer, the image can be =
scraped off=20
                                or lifted with tape and replaced with =
new=20
                                information. The use of chemical =
solvents is=20
                                another method which washes the ink from =
the=20
                                check and then the amount is altered or =
the=20
                                payee name is changed. It is important =
to=20
                                incorporate security features in checks =
because=20
                                the customer is held responsible for =
losses=20
                                incurred from the forged checks unless =
they can=20
                                show "due diligence". "Due diligence" =
means that=20
                                they must show that they have taken =
proper=20
                                precaution on their part to protect =
their=20
                                checks. This includes everything from=20
                                incorporating proper security features =
to proper=20
                                storage of checks.<BR>&nbsp;<BR>&nbsp;=20
                                =
</P></TD></TR></TBODY></TABLE></CENTER></DIV>
                              <DIV align=3Dcenter>
