                                <TR>
                                <TD vAlign=3Dtop width=3D399>
                                <P align=3Dcenter><IMG height=3D193=20
                                =
src=3D"http://glossary.ippaper.com/images/graphicsedviser/common/security=
/ProbCert.gif"=20
                                width=3D368 border=3D0> </P></TD>
                                <TD vAlign=3Dcenter width=3D208>
                                <P align=3Dcenter><B>Gift =
Certificates</B></P>
                                <P align=3Dleft>Gift certificates can be =
altered=20
                                in much the same way in which checks are =

                                altered. They may be duplicated or they =
can have=20
                                the name and dollar amounts altered. =
This could=20
                                result in a huge loss to a company if =
not=20
                                detected soon enough.=20
                              =
</P></TD></TR></TBODY></TABLE></CENTER></DIV>
                              <DIV align=3Dcenter>
                              <CENTER>
                              <TABLE cellSpacing=3D0 cellPadding=3D0 =
width=3D611=20
                              border=3D0>
                                <TBODY>
                                <TR>
                                <TD vAlign=3Dtop width=3D290>
                                <P =
align=3Dcenter><B><BR>&nbsp;<BR>Academic=20
                                Transcripts</B></P>
                                <P align=3Dleft>Transcripts have been =
altered by=20
                                students to show higher grades than what =
were=20
                                actually earned. Students alter their=20
                                transcripts to affect their eligibility =
into=20
                                another school or to mislead a =
prospective=20
                                employer when being considered for =
employment.=20
                                </P></TD>
                                <TD width=3D20></TD>
                                <TD vAlign=3Dtop width=3D290>
                                <P align=3Dcenter><B><BR>&nbsp;<BR>Event =

                                Tickets/Passes</B></P>
                                <P>Scalpers will duplicate passes or =
tickets to=20
                                events and then sell them for a profit. =
Not only=20
                                is this a type of counterfeiting and =
illegal, it=20
                                also can cause huge problems when large =
groups=20
                                of people come to an event and find =
their seats=20
                                have already been sold to another=20
                                person.<BR>&nbsp;<BR>&nbsp;=20
                                =
</P></TD></TR></TBODY></TABLE></CENTER></DIV>
                              <DIV align=3Dcenter>
                              <CENTER>
                              <TABLE cellSpacing=3D0 cellPadding=3D0 =
width=3D611=20
                              border=3D0>
                                <TBODY>
                                <TR>
                                <TD vAlign=3Dtop width=3D220>
                                <P align=3Dcenter><B>Prescription =
Pads</B></P>
                                <P align=3Dleft>Prescription blanks are =
forged and=20
                                duplicated for one basic reason, to =
obtain drugs=20
                                illegally. The quantity or number of =
refills for=20
                                the prescription may be altered, the =
type of=20
                                drug being prescribed is changed or the =
entire=20
                                prescription is duplicated. The forgery =
of=20
                                prescription blanks is accomplished much =
like=20
                                forgery of checks. They are duplicated =
by use of=20
                                computers, scanners, printers or =
copiers. They=20
                                can also be altered by the use of =
chemical=20
                                solvents to wash away the data and then =
that=20
                                data is replaced by false =
information.<BR>&nbsp;=20
                                </P></TD>
                                <TD vAlign=3Dcenter width=3D380>
                                <P align=3Dright><IMG height=3D236=20
                                =
src=3D"http://glossary.ippaper.com/images/graphicsedviser/common/security=
/ProbPrescrip.gif"=20
                                width=3D368 border=3D0> </P></TD></TR>
                                <TR>
                                <TD vAlign=3Dtop width=3D609 =
colSpan=3D2>&nbsp;=20
                                </TD></TR>
                                <TR>
                                <TD vAlign=3Dtop width=3D609 =
colSpan=3D2>
                                <P align=3Dcenter><B>Coupons</B></P>
                                <P align=3Dleft>Without proper security =
features,=20
                                coupons could be easily duplicated by =
using the=20
                                technology of the computers and output =
devices=20
                                that are available today. A restaurant =
owner may=20
                                distribute a "Free Dinner" coupon to =
promote the=20
                                opening of a new restaurant. If the =
coupon is=20
                                illegally duplicated and distributed to =
more=20
                                people than originally intended, the =
owner may=20
                                incur substantial losses. Consumer =
coupon fraud=20
                                is a big concern that needs to be dealt =
with but=20
                                along with consumer fraud is retail =
fraud.=20
                                Retail coupon fraud occurs when =
non-legitimate=20
                                retailers add in coupons that have not =
actually=20
                                been received through a consumer's =
purchase. One=20
                                way additional coupons are obtained is =
through=20
                                fraudulent duplication of the original =
coupons.=20
                                The counterfeit coupons are sent in with =
the=20
                                actual consumer coupons to the =
manufacturer for=20
                                redemption. Any business, from a private =

                                restaurant to a large company, could =
loose a=20
                                substantial amount from fraudulent=20
                                coupons.<BR>&nbsp;<BR>&nbsp;=20
                                =
</P></TD></TR></TBODY></TABLE></CENTER></DIV>
