                                <P align=3Dcenter><IMG height=3D214=20
                                =
src=3D"http://glossary.ippaper.com/images/graphicsedviser/common/security=
/CardsBadges.gif"=20
                                width=3D360 border=3D0> </P></TD>
                                <TD vAlign=3Dcenter width=3D234>
                                <P align=3Dcenter>&nbsp; <B>Membership =
Cards &amp;=20
                                Security Badges</B></P>
                                <P align=3Dleft>The forgery of =
membership cards,=20
                                passes, and security badges allows =
unauthorized=20
                                use and entrance into controlled =
environments.=20
                                This type of forgery not only results in =
dollar=20
                                loss, but can also result in the loss of =

                                security in protected areas. =
</P></TD></TR>
                                <TR>
                                <TD vAlign=3Dtop width=3D605 =
colSpan=3D2>
                                <P align=3Dcenter><B><BR>&nbsp;<BR>Legal =

                                Documents</B></P>
                                <P align=3Dleft>The authenticity of =
legal=20
                                documents can be tampered with when the =
proper=20
                                security features are not used to help =
protect=20
                                the document. Documents can be =
counterfeited or=20
                                the content, value, or ownership may be =
altered=20
                                by forgery of the documents. The =
tampering with=20
                                legal documents could cause incorrect=20
                                distribution of properties where =
individuals are=20
                                awarded ownership or given monies that =
are not=20
                                rightfully theirs. Information could be =
altered=20
                                so that rights and privileges are =
awarded to the=20
                                wrong individual, for example, if the =
name of a=20
                                person appointed power of attorney was =
changed=20
                                to a different individuals=20
                                name.<BR>&nbsp;<BR>&nbsp; </P></TD></TR>
                                <TR>
                                <TD vAlign=3Dbottom width=3D609 =
colSpan=3D2>
                                <DIV align=3Dcenter>
                                <TABLE class=3Dyellowtable =
cellSpacing=3D0=20
                                cellPadding=3D5 width=3D525 border=3D5>
                                <TBODY>
                                <TR>
                                <TD width=3D510>
                                <P align=3Dcenter>The examples above =
give you an=20
                                idea of the documents that have security =
issues=20
                                related to them. Forgery of negotiable =
or=20
                                confidential documents can cause major =
problems=20
                                for a company or an individual. The =
pages in=20
                                <B><A=20
                                =
href=3D"http://glossary.ippaper.com/default.asp?req=3Dknowledge/category/=
38">Security=20
                                Features</A></B> provide information on=20
                                different security options. Some of them =
are=20
                                overt (visible) features and some are =
covert=20
                                (invisible) features. A mixture of overt =
and=20
                                covert features can be used to help =
protect your=20
                                documents.=20
                                =
</P></TD></TR></TBODY></TABLE></DIV></TD></TR></TBODY></TABLE></DIV>
